[center][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Say what a character should do, and watch them do it in Night City.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center][size=3]Animation Tools is a small app for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url]. Pick a character, spawn them in front of V, type what they should do, and press Generate. [url=https://uthana.com]Uthana[/url] makes the motion from your words on the game's own skeleton, and the character plays it a minute later, in the running game. Every clip you make is kept, ready to play again or to pack into a mod.[/size][/center]

[center][size=3]Made by the team behind [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35421]REDcode[/url], which makes the same clips in VS Code.[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What it does[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Pick a character.[/b] The Trauma Team medic, a corpo plaza man or woman, or another character record on a man's or woman's body.[/*]
[*][b]Spawn.[/b] The character appears 3 m in front of V, facing you.[/*]
[*][b]Generate.[/b] Say what they should do, such as "stands relaxed, raises his right hand and waves hello", pick a length, and press Generate. The button shows each stage and the time while Uthana works. Feet stay on the ground: stepping, kicking and jumping are fine, floating and sliding are not. [b]Upper body only[/b] keeps the legs still for a wave or a phone call.[/*]
[*][b]Play it at once.[/b] The new clip is swapped into the running game and the character plays it. No restart.[/*]
[*][b]Your animations.[/b] The clips made for that character's body are listed, newest first, with their words. Pick one and Play, or Stop.[/*]
[*][b]Into a mod.[/b] Clips go into the project open in REDcode, so packing it makes a mod with them. With REDcode closed, they go into the app's own project in Documents\REDnode\Animation Tools.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url] 0.68.0 or later, with what it needs (RED4ext, redscript).[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url] 1.14 or later.[/*]
[*]REDbridge, which [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35421]REDcode[/url] installs for you.[/*]
[*]An [url=https://uthana.com]Uthana[/url] account and its key, set once in REDnode's or REDcode's Keys. Uthana charges about $0.10 a second of motion, only for a clip it finishes. Paying customers own what they make; Uthana may train on what you send and get back.[/*]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 on PC, [b]game version 2.5[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

Install it with your mod manager, or extract the zip into the game folder. Then switch [b]Animation Tools[/b] on in REDnode's Mod Manager.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Coming next[/color][/b][/size]

Making animations for V, and several takes of one clip to choose from.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Credits[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Uthana[/b] for the motion, from words.[/*]
[*][b]WolvenKit[/b], whose libraries in REDbridge read and write the game's animation files.[/*]
